{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2919","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2919","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2919\",\"parent_revision\":\"4200435032f9e966d2dc27b4ff9a94e9ebfd0d12\",\"root_revision\":\"1b700dc9fa9ac56ec655a14a5b737f761220a59152f728335cb53d8f9f0343fd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThree minor, non-blocking concerns from PR #2918 (redirect GitHub content store off the protected default branch to a dedicated dh-content branch), bundled as one concentrated follow-up since none is independently urgent:\\n\\n1. _content_branch() caches readiness per _GitHubContentsStore instance (self._branch_ready). A long-lived process holding a store instance across a MANUAL deletion of dh-content mid-session would not re-bootstrap and would fail on next write. No code path deletes the branch today, so this is latent, not live.\\n\\n2. dh-content accumulates full commit history forever with no GC/compaction story \u2014 identical to the previous default-branch design's characteristic, not a regression introduced by PR #2918, but worth addressing if .dh/content/v1/ write volume grows enough that branch size/clone time becomes a concern.\\n\\n3. create_git_ref's return type in the _ContentsRepository Protocol is object since no current caller uses the created ref's SHA \u2014 fine today, but a future caller wanting it would need the Protocol signature tightened.\\n\\nNone of these need to be fixed before or split out of #2918 \u2014 they're follow-up hardening for if/when this becomes load-bearing at higher volume.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor(backlog-mcp): dh-content branch hardening \u2014 gc/compaction story, manual-deletion re-bootstrap, protocol return type** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4cc4d1a2f3bd460934566e0fd35a333bcfc179d616d49bbad91a71592fcf09d9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPUXxTQ\"}"}